WEBVTT

00:01.050 --> 00:02.990
It summons magicite beasts.

00:04.260 --> 00:05.600
Ripple!

00:06.170 --> 00:08.000
I'm sorry!

00:09.410 --> 00:11.230
I can't keep this up anymore!

00:41.100 --> 00:44.060
<b><u>Reborn</u></b>

00:41.100 --> 00:44.060
<b>to Master the Blade
\h\h\h\h\hFrom Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire\h\h\h\h\h</b>

00:41.100 --> 00:44.060
<b>to Master the Blade
From Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire</b>

01:57.130 --> 02:02.050
<b>Episode 9          A New Artifact</b>

01:58.470 --> 02:00.220
My desk!

02:00.580 --> 02:01.780
It's huge!

02:01.780 --> 02:03.190
Be careful, Rani!

02:03.770 --> 02:09.370
It's probably as strong as Seilyn and Rahl 
were when they became magicite beasts!

02:09.370 --> 02:11.900
Your words and your face 
are telling two different stories!

02:11.900 --> 02:13.140
Oh, whoops.

02:20.190 --> 02:21.830
<i>It's a different color,</i>

02:21.830 --> 02:25.120
<i>but I feel the same flow of power 
as I did when I saw those heat rays.</i>

02:25.490 --> 02:26.700
<i>Which means...</i>

02:27.640 --> 02:30.460
It's probably going to fire 
heat rays everywhere!

02:31.110 --> 02:32.410
S-Stop it, please!

02:32.810 --> 02:34.260
Of course.

02:34.260 --> 02:36.880
The cafeteria's on the floor below!

02:36.880 --> 02:38.880
That's not what's important now!

02:41.820 --> 02:43.350
Maybe I can't stop it firing, but...

02:49.010 --> 02:51.810
She's so absurdly strong...

02:52.530 --> 02:54.430
Sorry, ma'am.

02:54.810 --> 02:58.400
I made a big hole in the roof.

02:58.400 --> 03:02.690
W-Well, that's not so bad...

03:03.070 --> 03:05.130
It's going to come back down, though.

03:05.540 --> 03:09.660
We need Artifacts to 
defeat a magicite beast.

03:11.550 --> 03:13.050
It's going to land in the schoolyard!

03:14.180 --> 03:16.000
When it does, I'll finish it off.

03:17.670 --> 03:18.960
Wait!

03:18.960 --> 03:23.130
Yua, it's dangerous there!

03:24.590 --> 03:26.590
Above you! Above you!

03:26.590 --> 03:28.600
Run away!

03:35.890 --> 03:36.810
Chop!

03:44.310 --> 03:46.730
Yua's amazing...

03:47.040 --> 03:49.390
<i>I may have already damaged it with my kick,</i>

03:49.390 --> 03:52.190
<i>but she still managed to chop it in half 
with a wave of her hand.</i>

03:52.540 --> 03:54.210
<i>She's as strong as I thought!</i>

03:55.300 --> 03:59.170
Will we not see any more 
magicite beasts for a while?

03:59.470 --> 04:03.490
Yes. We learned in the last battle

04:03.490 --> 04:07.700
that Ripple absorbs mana 
from Special-class Rune bearers

04:07.700 --> 04:10.130
and uses it to summon magicite beasts.

04:10.480 --> 04:13.880
And summoning that magicite beast 
drained the mana she'd built up.

04:14.460 --> 04:19.420
We won't see another one until 
her mana builds up again, right?

04:19.880 --> 04:22.220
You understand well.

04:22.220 --> 04:24.440
Um, I have another question.

04:25.060 --> 04:30.020
Why do all the summoned magicite beasts 
appear to be former demihumans?

04:30.290 --> 04:33.760
Probably because Ripple 
herself is a demihuman.

04:34.130 --> 04:38.670
Demihumans have what you 
might call a sixth sense.

04:39.240 --> 04:41.220
It's said they could even use telepathy.

04:41.220 --> 04:46.680
She's using that species-wide 
connection to summon them.

04:46.680 --> 04:48.770
Is that why?

04:48.770 --> 04:52.880
Which is why what they did 
could only be done to Ripple.

04:53.260 --> 04:58.090
It's even possible they created a demihuman 
Hyral Menas specifically for this purpose.

04:58.460 --> 05:01.780
I feel bad for Ripple,

05:01.780 --> 05:03.830
having her friends used in such a way.

05:04.230 --> 05:08.130
A lot of Highlanders don't see people 
on the surface as their equals,

05:08.130 --> 05:10.330
which leads to this way of thinking.

05:10.870 --> 05:12.780
It's embarrassing.

05:12.780 --> 05:14.360
Now, now, everyone.

05:14.360 --> 05:15.780
It's all in how you think about it!

05:16.170 --> 05:19.790
My comrades have been stuck 
as magicite beasts all this time,

05:19.790 --> 05:21.750
so this way, we can finally let them rest.

05:22.060 --> 05:24.490
As long as nobody around us gets hurt.

05:25.470 --> 05:29.850
Of course! We'll make sure they don't!

05:32.050 --> 05:34.110
Thanks, everyone.

05:34.110 --> 05:35.140
Excuse me.

05:35.710 --> 05:37.090
Come in!

05:39.400 --> 05:40.970
Brother Raf!

05:40.970 --> 05:41.870
Eris!

05:42.070 --> 05:43.880
I've been worried about you.

05:43.880 --> 05:45.470
Tell me how you're doing later.

05:45.470 --> 05:47.080
Right now, we have urgent news.

05:47.080 --> 05:50.280
Is something wrong, you two?

05:50.520 --> 05:53.740
The neighboring country of Venefic 
has violated our borders.

05:54.130 --> 05:58.930
Prince Wein is asking for Sir Theodore 
to return to the castle immediately.

06:00.040 --> 06:03.920
<b>Two Weeks Later</b>

06:02.190 --> 06:03.920
What a great bath!

06:04.890 --> 06:08.960
I'm glad nothing happened 
when we were on duty today!

06:08.960 --> 06:11.390
I think one person here 
would disagree with you.

06:12.230 --> 06:15.530
We haven't seen a single 
magicite beast since then!

06:15.530 --> 06:17.210
That's a good thing!

06:17.210 --> 06:19.670
You're right, but...

06:19.670 --> 06:23.840
Don't you think we need a place where 
we can show off the results of our training?

06:23.840 --> 06:25.430
I don't think that, no.

06:25.430 --> 06:28.980
It's better for Ripple that nothing happens.

06:29.410 --> 06:31.410
I get that, but...

06:31.700 --> 06:35.370
Liselotte, have you heard 
what's going on near the border?

06:35.680 --> 06:40.320
There's a standoff going on right now, 
I heard. But nothing beyond that...

06:40.320 --> 06:44.670
So the Prismer's still not 
doing anything either, huh?

06:46.330 --> 06:50.510
That's the kind of sigh you make 
when the one you like won't notice you.

06:50.510 --> 06:55.720
Well, Chris does say her 
ideal type is a Prismer.

06:55.720 --> 07:01.200
It always feels like Chris is a totally 
different person on the inside and outside.

07:01.200 --> 07:02.160
Yes.

07:02.160 --> 07:05.140
Her body is Boobs, but her brain is Muscles.

07:05.830 --> 07:06.860
Yua!

07:06.860 --> 07:09.760
<i>I couldn't even sense her approach.</i>

07:09.760 --> 07:11.030
<i>Impressive!</i>

07:11.030 --> 07:12.050
<i>Wait...</i>

07:12.050 --> 07:14.090
<i>If there aren't any magicite beasts...</i>

07:14.570 --> 07:15.840
Yua!

07:16.330 --> 07:20.890
The way you chopped that magicite 
beast in half was amazing!

07:20.890 --> 07:23.910
I'd love it if you could 
show me how it was done!

07:23.910 --> 07:25.870
In a battle, preferably!

07:25.870 --> 07:26.610
I refuse.

07:26.610 --> 07:28.290
Why?

07:28.830 --> 07:30.510
I don't like physical exercise.

07:30.740 --> 07:32.900
Well, it's hard for me to respond to that...

07:32.900 --> 07:35.670
What can I do to make you tell me?

07:37.400 --> 07:38.800
Yua?

07:39.190 --> 07:41.730
There's something I want you 
to teach me, too.

07:41.730 --> 07:44.950
If you do, I'll fight you, 
or do anything else you want.

07:44.950 --> 07:46.400
Really?

07:46.400 --> 07:47.660
What is it?

07:47.660 --> 07:50.270
I'll teach you anything you want to know!

07:50.270 --> 07:53.160
How can I get my boobs that big, too?

07:54.370 --> 07:58.330
Um, well... mine kinda just grew this way.

07:58.330 --> 08:00.360
That doesn't tell me anything.

08:00.360 --> 08:02.810
I want to have huge boobs 
so everyone likes me!

08:03.170 --> 08:06.290
I want to show off my cleavage 
to the entire world, like you do, Boobs!

08:06.620 --> 08:08.990
I don't do that!

08:08.990 --> 08:13.820
If you can teach me a way 
to make my breasts bigger,

08:13.820 --> 08:15.770
I'll fight you as much as you want!

08:16.040 --> 08:17.730
Leone!

08:17.730 --> 08:20.120
I-I don't know either!

08:20.120 --> 08:23.180
Plus, they're heavy, they make your 
shoulders stiff, and people stare!

08:23.180 --> 08:24.480
There's nothing good about them.

08:24.480 --> 08:27.300
You're lucky you get 
to worry about that stuff!

08:27.300 --> 08:29.730
You don't know how us flat girls live!

08:30.330 --> 08:33.910
So Rafinha's taking Yua's side?

08:33.910 --> 08:38.010
You don't have to worry, 
because you've got proper boobs.

08:38.010 --> 08:40.050
And they're not big enough 
to strain your shoulders.

08:40.050 --> 08:42.340
In a way, they're the best size.

08:42.340 --> 08:44.700
I don't know about that...

08:45.120 --> 08:48.910
And you don't have to deal with 
Lyn playing around in there.

08:48.910 --> 08:52.230
I think Liselotte ought to 
experience that at least once.

08:54.310 --> 08:56.000
Go, Lyn!

08:58.340 --> 09:02.490
N-No! It tickles!

09:02.490 --> 09:03.770
Hey!

09:03.770 --> 09:07.370
Somebody help me!

09:08.020 --> 09:10.830
Liselotte was really mad...

09:10.830 --> 09:14.250
She was intense. I was scared.

09:14.250 --> 09:16.120
Rafinha!

09:16.920 --> 09:19.150
I have something to give to you!

09:19.580 --> 09:23.380
Change into your uniform and come 
to the principal's office, would you?

09:25.600 --> 09:28.810
Theodore says this is for you.

09:29.670 --> 09:32.990
I this a new Artifact?

09:32.990 --> 09:38.690
Yes. It has the same base as 
your current "Shiny Flow,"

09:38.690 --> 09:41.770
but it's an upgraded version 
with a second Gift as well.

09:41.770 --> 09:44.420
Wow! Thank you!

09:44.750 --> 09:50.130
I'm surprised Theodore has any time to make 
Artifacts, with how busy he is right now,

09:50.130 --> 09:52.140
but this is a great help!

09:52.410 --> 09:53.420
Yes!

09:53.420 --> 10:00.620
Also, the second power that 
Artifact has is one of healing.

10:01.210 --> 10:04.570
I've never heard of an Artifact 
with that kind of power!

10:04.570 --> 10:09.030
It's quite rare and difficult to make.

10:09.030 --> 10:12.480
That's why he wants you to have it, he says.

10:13.780 --> 10:15.570
Theodore...

10:15.570 --> 10:21.480
He also asks that you take care 
of Ripple for him.

10:21.820 --> 10:22.850
Of course!

10:22.850 --> 10:26.340
I'll protect Ripple and everyone else!

10:26.340 --> 10:29.920
I'll have to start training right now 
so that I can use it properly!

10:29.920 --> 10:31.450
Sure you do.

10:31.450 --> 10:36.330
Chris, you always make that face 
whenever Theodore is involved!

10:36.330 --> 10:38.580
I am not making a face.

10:43.150 --> 10:44.420
That's...

10:45.790 --> 10:47.540
Hurry and put out the fire!

10:47.540 --> 10:50.510
The magicite beast has been defeated. 
The flames need putting out, now!

10:51.070 --> 10:52.540
What's going on?

10:53.130 --> 10:54.470
Principal Miliera!

10:55.530 --> 10:57.910
Ripple summoned more magicite beasts.

10:57.910 --> 11:01.680
We sealed them in a pocket space 
and fought them, but...

11:02.380 --> 11:03.530
Silva!

11:04.480 --> 11:05.360
Silva!

11:05.730 --> 11:07.160
Silva?

11:10.890 --> 11:12.940
He's horribly wounded...

11:14.270 --> 11:15.220
I'm fine.

11:15.740 --> 11:18.640
Forget about me, and get Ripple out of here.

11:19.050 --> 11:21.240
I can't let her see me like this.

11:21.850 --> 11:23.570
Make sure she's safe!

11:23.570 --> 11:24.250
Okay!

11:25.240 --> 11:30.280
For someone as strong as you 
to be this badly injured...

11:30.280 --> 11:32.650
It must have been a powerful 
magicite beast indeed.

11:33.150 --> 11:36.960
I'm so sorry... It was my failure.

11:36.960 --> 11:39.920
No! It's not your fault!

11:39.920 --> 11:41.430
It's their fault!

11:41.770 --> 11:42.990
"Their fault"?

11:44.430 --> 11:45.740
I'm sorry...

11:46.790 --> 11:48.970
Rati... Pram?

11:48.970 --> 11:50.320
What happened?

11:51.190 --> 11:55.890
He protected me when a magicite 
beast was about to kill me...

11:55.890 --> 11:56.920
and he was badly hurt.

11:57.550 --> 12:02.600
N-No! Rati tried to protect <i>me</i>!

12:02.600 --> 12:04.440
So it's my fault!

12:04.440 --> 12:05.730
I'm so sorry!

12:05.730 --> 12:07.640
"Sorry" won't cut it!

12:07.640 --> 12:10.210
Thanks to you, Silva is...

12:10.210 --> 12:11.390
Stop.

12:11.920 --> 12:16.450
My lack of care when activating the pocket 
space caused them to be caught up in it.

12:16.450 --> 12:17.870
The mistake was all mine.

12:18.170 --> 12:22.250
And as someone with power,

12:22.250 --> 12:25.300
it's my job to protect 
the powerless Runeless.

12:26.130 --> 12:27.630
Were you hurt?

12:27.630 --> 12:30.250
No. Not even a scratch.

12:30.610 --> 12:32.040
I see.

12:32.040 --> 12:33.690
Then...

12:34.720 --> 12:35.980
Silva?

12:36.490 --> 12:38.690
Silva! Silva!

12:39.090 --> 12:41.340
Oh, no! We need to hurry and 
get him to the medical room!

12:41.340 --> 12:42.660
Wait!

12:43.860 --> 12:45.600
I'll try and help.

12:46.000 --> 12:47.520
The healing Gift...

12:48.240 --> 12:49.570
Please, go ahead!

12:49.880 --> 12:50.940
Okay!

12:50.940 --> 12:52.250
You'll be okay.

12:52.250 --> 12:53.540
You can do it, Rani.

13:05.320 --> 13:07.020
Does anything feel "wrong"?

13:07.020 --> 13:08.190
Yes.

13:08.190 --> 13:13.410
That's good. It means that your power is 
flowing to a different Gift than usual.

13:13.410 --> 13:15.100
Please continue.

13:15.780 --> 13:18.360
Focus on what lies just 
beyond your fingertips.

13:18.360 --> 13:19.580
Okay...

13:20.150 --> 13:22.480
<i>So this is the healing Gift...</i>

13:23.300 --> 13:28.150
<i>The movements of the mana are so complex, 
I don't think I could easily recreate it...</i>

13:29.510 --> 13:33.640
Now hold that light up to Silva.

13:33.640 --> 13:34.780
Okay!

13:42.920 --> 13:43.870
His wounds...

13:44.440 --> 13:46.170
They're healing!

13:48.570 --> 13:52.260
<i>So the healing Gift places 
a heavy strain on its user?</i>

13:52.710 --> 13:53.620
<i>Then...</i>

13:56.510 --> 13:58.350
Rani. I'll help you.

13:58.710 --> 14:01.550
<i>I can't copy the mana the Gift uses.</i>

14:01.550 --> 14:04.090
<i>But if I just create mana with 
a wavelength similar to Rani's...</i>

14:04.090 --> 14:05.370
Chris?

14:05.770 --> 14:07.140
Think you can do it?

14:07.140 --> 14:10.020
Yeah! I can do a lot more now!

14:23.770 --> 14:25.790
He's okay now, isn't he?

14:25.790 --> 14:28.130
Thank you both.

14:28.130 --> 14:30.650
Now, get him to the medical room.

14:30.650 --> 14:31.550
Okay!

14:32.530 --> 14:35.380
Thank you for saving Silva.

14:35.380 --> 14:39.430
No... Anyone would have done the same.

14:41.370 --> 14:44.140
Thanks, Chris! You were a huge help!

15:01.530 --> 15:04.190
Are the two of you okay?

15:04.190 --> 15:05.270
We're fine...

15:05.570 --> 15:07.430
Really?

15:07.430 --> 15:08.980
That's...

15:09.250 --> 15:11.430
The super-spicy meal!

15:11.770 --> 15:14.400
It's so spicy!

15:14.400 --> 15:16.240
But it's good!

15:16.240 --> 15:18.090
It sure wakes you up, huh?

15:18.400 --> 15:22.560
Super-spicy food reminds me of home, though.

15:22.790 --> 15:24.780
Where did you say you were from?

15:25.560 --> 15:27.470
Alucard, in the north.

15:28.210 --> 15:32.150
It's cold up there, so you eat 
spicy food to warm yourself up.

15:32.690 --> 15:35.570
So we're used to eating really spicy food.

15:35.570 --> 15:38.900
It reminds us of home!

15:39.290 --> 15:41.120
You want some too, then?

15:41.410 --> 15:44.070
I'd love some, but... there's so much...

15:44.400 --> 15:47.050
I'll give you some of mine.

15:47.390 --> 15:50.080
Th-Thanks...

15:50.080 --> 15:52.000
Give me some too, Inglis!

15:52.000 --> 15:53.700
Sure thing!

15:53.700 --> 15:54.720
No!

15:55.130 --> 15:56.550
Why?

15:56.550 --> 15:58.930
No indirect kisses!

15:58.930 --> 16:01.450
Sure, sure. Got it.

16:02.040 --> 16:05.140
You're just doing what Pram 
tells you today, huh?

16:05.490 --> 16:09.100
Well, I did kinda screw up yesterday.

16:09.100 --> 16:11.440
I owe you guys a big thank-you, too.

16:11.440 --> 16:14.710
No, it's not your fault!

16:14.710 --> 16:17.540
You just tried to help me...

16:17.540 --> 16:20.910
But I had to be saved 
by somebody else instead!

16:21.490 --> 16:24.610
I need to apologize to Silva.

16:24.610 --> 16:29.090
I don't think he was mad, though.

16:29.090 --> 16:31.870
Yeah. He was sticking up for you.

16:31.870 --> 16:38.560
He was kind of a jerk when we first met, 
so I thought he just hated squires.

16:38.560 --> 16:40.600
Oh, I get it!

16:40.600 --> 16:43.770
He must be one of those guys 
who likes young boys!

16:44.260 --> 16:46.730
That's why he was so kind to Rati!

16:46.730 --> 16:47.730
Well?

16:47.730 --> 16:50.050
That can't be right!

16:50.050 --> 16:53.700
Yeah, I really can't handle any more rivals!

16:53.970 --> 16:57.000
So why was he so harsh on me?

16:57.830 --> 17:02.360
Cause you're a girl, Chris! Obviously!

17:02.360 --> 17:05.020
He just likes young boys...

17:05.020 --> 17:08.090
I'd prefer you didn't jump to 
conclusions about people like that.

17:08.520 --> 17:10.390
Silva?

17:10.390 --> 17:12.480
Are you feeling better?

17:12.480 --> 17:15.040
Yes. The scars are almost all gone, too.

17:15.040 --> 17:16.750
That Gift of yours is incredible.

17:16.750 --> 17:20.230
Um, I'm so sorry about yesterday.

17:20.230 --> 17:22.060
We're really sorry.

17:23.380 --> 17:26.520
Don't worry about it. It was 
my mistake to begin with.

17:27.860 --> 17:31.930
And in the end, you were 
the ones who saved me.

17:32.280 --> 17:34.770
Let me apologize for my rudeness 
and thank you properly.

17:35.580 --> 17:36.410
Thank you.

17:39.520 --> 17:42.940
Not at all... I'm sorry we were such brats!

17:43.370 --> 17:44.930
I'm sorry!

17:45.620 --> 17:49.800
Now we've all apologized, 
so we're even, right?

17:55.000 --> 17:55.840
Yes.

17:56.380 --> 17:57.700
Let's say that we are.

18:02.380 --> 18:04.590
Okay, your turn's over, Rani.

18:04.590 --> 18:06.100
My turn now.

18:09.260 --> 18:10.810
We ate a whole lot!

18:10.810 --> 18:12.700
Let's do our best to defend 
Ripple this afternoon!

18:12.700 --> 18:16.370
Sure, but since Silva and his group 
defeated the magicite beast,

18:16.370 --> 18:19.880
we won't see another for a while.

18:21.540 --> 18:23.760
Chris...

18:23.760 --> 18:25.430
They can't do this!

18:27.180 --> 18:28.280
Come in!

18:29.920 --> 18:31.340
Excuse us.

18:31.340 --> 18:34.020
It's time for our shift to begin.

18:34.810 --> 18:36.630
Thanks for coming.

18:37.020 --> 18:40.340
Um. It sounds like something 
had upset you...

18:40.340 --> 18:43.640
Oh, I'm sorry. I couldn't help myself.

18:44.080 --> 18:46.580
Actually, the Royal Guard sent a demand to us

18:46.580 --> 18:50.480
that we turn Ripple over 
to them for protection.

18:51.790 --> 18:53.940
Why now, after everything?

18:53.940 --> 19:00.850
They say they're sending Ripple back to the 
Highland and getting a new Hyral Menas.

19:01.590 --> 19:07.680
But... You can't replace her just 
because she's a little sick...

19:07.680 --> 19:09.760
That's treating her like 
an object, not a person!

19:10.520 --> 19:14.210
We will continue to keep 
her safe at the academy.

19:15.240 --> 19:16.510
Right?

19:16.980 --> 19:21.250
But, Miliera, if you get into 
a fight with the Royal Guard,

19:21.250 --> 19:23.210
won't that cause problems for everyone?

19:23.210 --> 19:25.940
Not in the least.

19:25.940 --> 19:29.940
Protecting you is what we all want to do.

19:30.230 --> 19:32.900
She's right!

19:32.900 --> 19:35.140
Leave it to us!

19:36.580 --> 19:37.700
Guys...

19:42.150 --> 19:45.400
Prism Flow? Now of all times?

19:45.960 --> 19:50.510
The magicite beasts don't care 
what we've got going on in our lives.

19:50.510 --> 19:55.120
What's the principal 
going to do about Ripple?

19:55.540 --> 20:00.800
She's sending a formal message to 
Prince Wein, as a means of buying time.

20:00.800 --> 20:05.680
That's why Rati and Pram 
ran off in the Flying Gears.

20:06.680 --> 20:09.430
The prince is away right now.

20:09.430 --> 20:11.410
It's bad timing.

20:11.410 --> 20:16.350
They were excited to make up 
for their failure before, though.

20:17.090 --> 20:18.320
What's wrong?

20:19.230 --> 20:21.780
Bad timing...

20:22.890 --> 20:26.170
Oh, well, there's nothing 
we can do about the rain.

20:26.960 --> 20:32.950
No, I mean the way the Royal Guard is 
doing this when Prince Wein isn't around.

20:32.950 --> 20:36.700
If somebody is pulling strings 
behind the scenes...

20:40.260 --> 20:41.090
Leone!

20:41.090 --> 20:42.330
On it!

20:51.870 --> 20:53.470
A lightning beast...

20:55.190 --> 20:58.820
That's the power of my brother's Artifact!

21:31.430 --> 21:33.290
Brother Leon!

21:33.290 --> 21:36.440
Hey. It's been a long time, Leone.

21:37.320 --> 21:38.670
Wait!

21:41.200 --> 21:43.150
Somebody else is here.

21:53.360 --> 21:54.830
Who's there?!

22:02.700 --> 22:03.830
It can't be...

22:07.660 --> 22:09.470
The Bloodchain Brigade!

23:45.070 --> 23:50.060
Silva is
 a rival,
 too?

23:45.070 --> 23:50.060
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

23:45.070 --> 23:50.060
That's
imposs-
ible!

